From: Comzee <117947104+Comzee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: preserve RK3128 reference board GPIO handoff on restart

The shipped u-boot panel initializer requires the legacy rockchip,rk-fb,
lcdc alias and power_ctr DT entries. Our mainline DT has none. Returning
from the GPIO-owning driver to an older confirmed/rescue kernel using
panel-lvds otherwise leaves reset asserted and panel enable inactive.
The old kernel drives a healthy DRM scanout into an electrically off panel.

Keep the active GPIO levels across restart, including either DRM/platform
shutdown order. Userspace can have unprepared the panel before reboot, so
platform shutdown reestablishes the vendor active sequence unconditionally.
Runtime disable, driver removal, halt and poweroff retain the vendor inverse
sequence. There is no change to GPIO acquisition or vendor delays.

References: shipped Image rk_disp_pwr_enable 0xc02fe508, disable 0xc02fe630;
shipped u-boot LCD init 0x6001e268, legacy parser 0x6001de64, GPIO power
list 0x6001dcd0/0x6001de20. See docs/research/black-panel.md.

Signed-off-by: Comzee <117947104+Comzee@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-rk3128-reference.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-rk3128-reference.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
  */
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
@@ -59,6 +60,10 @@
 static int rk3128_reference_panel_unprepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 {
 	struct rk3128_reference_panel *reference = to_rk3128_reference_panel(panel);
+
+	/* A reboot must hand an active panel to kernels without GPIO ownership. */
+	if (system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART)
+		return 0;
 
 	/* Vendor disable uses the same order, inverted levels, no delays. */
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(reference->reset, 1);
@@ -146,6 +151,19 @@
 {
 	struct rk3128_reference_panel *reference = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	/*
+	 * The shipped bootloader cannot reinitialize panel GPIOs from our
+	 * mainline DT. Older confirmed/rescue kernels use panel-lvds and leave
+	 * these lines untouched. Restore the vendor active sequence even if
+	 * userspace unprepared us before SYSTEM_RESTART, then leave it active.
+	 * The unprepare guard also covers a later DRM consumer shutdown.
+	 */
+	if (system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART) {
+		if (rk3128_reference_panel_prepare(&reference->panel))
+			dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to hand off active panel on restart\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/* The DRM consumer may already have disabled/unprepared us. */
 	if (reference->panel.enabled)
 		drm_panel_disable(&reference->panel);
